{
    "_comment": [
        "presetKits are kits picked inside a soundfont, \"<file>#<bank>:<program>\": a General MIDI font's acoustic kits sit at bank 128 (FluidR3: Jazz 32, Brush 40, Standard 0, Room 8, Power 16, Orchestra 48: its timpani span keys 41–53, so the \"Orchestra\" entry puts timpani C on TOM and G on HAT, the triangle on OPEN, the concert crash on CYMBAL, the tambourine on PERC; castanets stay on CLAP; the \"Cumbia\" entries put the güiro on PERC, a timbale on TOM, the cowbell (campana) on CYMBAL, a conga (llamador) on CLAP); \"?CYMBAL=51&HAT=44\" after it picks a row's key (the ride and the hi-hat foot for jazz), see DrumKit.",
        "The machines and the engines they play. Each plays on its own sketchpad track (0-9) and",
        "Zynthian channel (0-15). drumMachines are page 1's: engine.soundfont is the default kit, any",
        "soundfont in kitFolder can replace it (tap the nameplate); rows are read from the kit itself",
        "(eight roles: KICK SNARE CLAP TOM HAT OPEN CYMBAL PERC). machines are the rest, by kind:",
        "'mono' (a one-note-per-step line with accents and slides: bass, lead) or 'chords'. For each:",
        "engine.controls sets plugin ports (an alternative source's are where its MODS knobs start);",
        "the SOUND MODIFIERS (MODS) of every engine are in engines.json, by engine (EngineProfiles);",
        "presets is its presets file (in scale degrees); defaultPreset is what a fresh",
        "machine starts with; baseNote is degree 1 at octave 0 (before the root).",
        "'sampler' is page 5's SAMPLE KING: no engine, it plays samples on libzynthbox's SamplerSynth (track 6, slot notes from baseNote up).",
        "sampleFolders are where the sampler's LOAD looks for audio files (recursively)."
    ],
